0 48 155 [
[(Here we combine three parabolic waves \050in the same way as, two patches ago, we combined)]
[(sawtooth waves\051. The parabolic wave is obtained from the sawtooth wave \050assuming it)]
[(runs from -0.5 to 0.5\051 by the formula: y=x*x/2 - 1/12. This is normalized so that the)]
[(corner has a slope change of minus one unit per cycle, and adjusted to remove any DC)]
[(component.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
